    #Story 1 
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/04_story_1.png"
    "Story 1: A Girl Awakens"

    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/05_chamber_1.png"
    coffinLikeMachine "— Repeat: Error in dormant state of specimen."
    coffinLikeMachine "Accommodation of specimen no longer possible. Awakening processes activated."
    coffinLikeMachine "Blood exchange complete. Line breaker severed. Sea of Origin discharge...complete."
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/06_chamber_2.png"
    coffinLikeMachine "Removing particles..."
    coffinLikeMachine "Specimen beginning to awaken. All vital signs normal."
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/07_chamber_3.png"
    coffinLikeMachine "Particle removal complete. Opening accommodation chamber. All nearby staff members are advised to keep their distance."
    scene image  "12_mist_on_the_waster/08_chamber_4.png"
 
    "The girl awakens to find her mind a perfect blank."
    "She knows not where she is. Who she is."
    "She does not even know if these are questions worth asking."
    "She hears a voice; almost a faint scream."
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/09_begin.png"
    "'I must go there.'"
    "She knows not where 'there' is, yet she begins to walk all the same."
    "She moves down the corridor as if the voice drives her."

    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/10_encounter.png"
    "Along the path, she finds a large crystal in the shape of a person."
    "Her hand, acting of its own accord, reaches out for the strange object."

    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/11_memory.png"
    "Images flood her mind; memories left within the crystal."
    
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/10_encounter.png" # refer to prev images
    "And through these memories, she suddenly understands."
    "This crystal is the corpse of a girl—a girl of the same type as herself."
    "We were created to be weapons."
    
    #Page 1
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/12_note.png"
    "- Halting of Production and Project Suspension -"
    
    "As of tomorrow (June 8), the cloning-oriented weaponry mass-production project we have worked on thus far will cease any and all activity following the manufacture of sister unit 123 and the project itself will be shelved.
    I will share the reasons for this decision later on, but allow me to say here and now that I assume full responsibility."
    
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/13_enemy_encounter.png"

    "An eerie sound slithers from the soles of her feet."
    "A white aberration appears, its state of matter undefined."
    "Sensing its hostility, the girl's eyes turn red."
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/14_enemy_killed.png"
    "The girl dispatches the white creature."
    "She fought with such agility, it seems impossible to think she is so newly awakened."
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/15_continue.png"
    "Her composure flawless, the girl continues down the hall."
  
    "The voice in her head drives her on relentlessly."
    "She finds herself in a darkness devoid of life."
    "Yet she continues on in search of answers."
    #Story 1 end
    

    #carrier "Ah, so this is the tale of a girl created to be a weapon."
    #levania "What the—!?"
    #carrier "Good heavens! It ran off!"
    #levania "Explain this."
    #carrier "I, er, fear I have never seen a scarecrow take flight in such a fashion before."
    #carrier "It would seem they are capable of moving."
    #levania "Ugh. How annoying."
    #levania "If it runs again, I will kill it."
    #carrier "I'm not even certain you CAN kill it. It's made of a very strange substance."
    #carrier "Oh, at last!"
    #levania "Stand back while I tear this blasted thing to ribbons."
    
    #Story 2 Start
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/16_story_2.png"
    "Story 2: Crystallize"
    
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/17_establishing_shot.png"
    "The girl traverses a corridor filled with rubble."
    "A fight happened here."
    "She spies a faint light filtering in through the collapsed ceiling."
    "The girl climbs the rubble, seeking the light's source."

    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/18_plants.png"
    "Having climbed the wreckage, she spies row upon row of living plants."
    "The light spilling into the corridor below had been for their benefit."
    "Enraptured at the sight of the plants, the girl is suddenly beset by a terrible vertigo."
    
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/19_mind.png"
    "Her vision spins. Her mind reels."

    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/20_continue.png"
    "But she somehow manages to brush these feelings aside and continue her journey."
    
    #Note
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/21_note.png"
    "- Memory-Degradation Phenomenon Experiment Report -
    
    Specimens: 31, 33, 34, 35
    
    Procedure: Specimen 31 was shown a paper with an image of a blue square before being euthanized. The remaining three specimens were made to recover 31's memories from her body at staggered intervals afterward, at which point they were asked about the shape and color of the image on the paper."
    
    "Situation A: One Day Post-Death (Specimen: 33)
    Specimen 33: 'square'
    Specimen 33: 'blue'"
    
    "Situation B: Two Days Post-Death (Specimen: 34)
    Specimen 34: 'square'
    Specimen 34: 'gray'"
    
    "Situation C: Four Days Post-Death (Specimen: 35)
    Specimen 35: 'I don't know.'"
    
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/20_continue.png" # refer to prev image
    ""
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/22_enemy_encunter.png"
    "An aberration once again appears to block her progress."
    "She stares down her enemy with red eyes and utterly flawless composure."
    "The white phantom evaporates like so much mist."
    
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/23_statue.png"
    "These corpses were weapons like her—she might have even called them her 'sisters.'"
    "She holds up a hand up to the crystal and closes her eyes."
    
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/24_memory.png"
    "A torrent of images race forth and swallow the girl's consciousness."
    "They are memories. And they are horrible."
    "Girls—her sisters—overrun by a horde of aberrations."
    "Their pain and agony floods though her mind."
    "The white aberrations brought ruin to the facility."
  
    #Interaction door password here.
    #- Forgotten Letter: About the Gate's Passcode -
    #(This missive is written on paper for security reasons. Please dispose of it after reading.)
    #"You may have heard news of this already, but specimen 0—the original—will be granted permission to visit the cultivation labs, so we need to revise our security protocols with that in mind. I went ahead and changed the passcode, and I decided to make it related to the memory-degradation experiment report. All you need to do is input the shapes"
    #"You may have heard news of this already, but specimen 0—the original—will be granted permission to visit the cultivation labs, so we need to revise our security protocols with that in mind. I went ahead and changed the passcode, and I decided to make it related to the memory-degradation experiment report. All you need to do is input the shapes in specimens 35, 34, and 33's responses in that exact order. That's right, it's the opposite order they come in compared to the report itself, so make special note of that. Oh, and input "x" for "I don't know.""
    
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/23_statue.png"
    "Having inherited the memories, the girl moves on."
    "She must learn more. She must appease the voice in her head."
    
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/25_mr_monster.png"
    carrier "Ah, interesting. So this girl—this living weapon goes about collecting memories, mmm?"
    fio "*huff* *huff*"
    levania "Shouldn't you rest or...something?"
    fio "I'm okay..."
    levania "Listen to me: If you die, I don't get to eat any more of your dreams."
    levania "So stay alive until I'm done—then you can do as you like. Got it?"
    fio "*huff* Got it!"
    scene image "12_mist_on_the_waster/26_playing_water.png"
    levania "Let's stop and rest here for a bit."
    fio "*huff* You mean it?"
    levania "You wanted to play in the water, right? Well... knock yourself out."
    fio "Yaaay! Oh, thank you, Mr. Monster! Thank you!"
    carrier "Are you certain we have the time to dawdle like this?"
    levania "She's feeling down. It concerns me."
    carrier "You don't say..."
    levania "Did you see that?"
    carrier "Hmmm?"
    fio "Hey, Mr. Monster?"
    fio "When you become human, will you still be my friend?"
    carrier "Right then, that's the end of playtime! Time to be moving on!"
    levania "Feeling better?"
    fio "Yeah, lots!"
    fio "Thanks again, Mr. Monster."
    carrier "I see the next scarecrow!"
    levania "Don't you go anywhere."
    fio "Okey dokey!"
    
